/* Banca di domande, verificata il 16/11/2026. Generata da strumenti/banche.py: non modificare a mano. */
window.DIG_BANK = {"aree":["Informazioni e dati","Comunicazione e collaborazione","Sicurezza","Creazione di contenuti","Risoluzione di problemi","Tecnologie emergenti"],"q":[["dg1-001",0,"You type \"annual report 2023\" in quotation marks into a search engine. What is the effect of the quotation marks?",["The engine looks for pages containing that exact phrase","The engine hides pages that contain that phrase","The engine searches only the titles of the pages","The engine returns only PDF files and documents"],"Le virgolette impongono la frase esatta. La trappola è pensare che limitino il tipo di file o il campo di ricerca: quello lo fanno altri operatori.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 1, competence 1.1)",1,0],["dg1-002",0,"You search for \"jaguar -car\". What does the minus sign do?",["It excludes pages that contain the word car","It makes the engine search for car only","It marks car as the most important word","It limits results to pages written long ago"],"Il segno meno davanti a una parola la esclude dai risultati. Le altre opzioni invertono o inventano il significato dell'operatore.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.1)",1,0],["dg1-003",0,"Which search query returns results only from the europa.eu domain?",["budget site:europa.eu","budget in:europa.eu","budget +europa.eu only","budget #europa.eu"],"site: è l'operatore che limita la ricerca a un dominio. Gli altri sono simboli inventati o usati in altri servizi.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.1)",1,0],["dg1-004",0,"Which query is best for finding PDF reports about migration on EU institution websites?",["site:europa.eu filetype:pdf migration report","europa.eu -filetype:pdf migration report","filetype:europa.eu site:pdf migration report","migration report OR europa.eu AND pdf"],"Servono site: per il dominio e filetype: per il formato. La seconda opzione esclude i PDF, la terza scambia gli operatori, la quarta non filtra nulla.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.1)",3,0],["dg1-005",0,"You need an official statistic on unemployment in the EU. Which source is the most reliable?",["The dataset published by Eurostat","A blog post that quotes the figure","A widely shared social media post","A forum answer with many votes"],"Una fonte primaria istituzionale è più affidabile di una citazione di seconda mano. Popolarità e condivisioni non misurano l'accuratezza.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.2)",1,0],["dg1-006",0,"What does \"lateral reading\" mean when you evaluate an unfamiliar website?",["Leaving the site to see what other sources say about it","Reading the whole site from the last page to the first","Reading only the headlines and skipping the text","Comparing the site with its translated versions"],"La lettura laterale significa uscire dalla pagina e verificare l'autore e il sito su altre fonti. Leggere di più la stessa pagina non ne verifica l'affidabilità.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.2)",2,0],["dg1-007",0,"Two colleagues type the same words into the same search engine and see different results. What is the most likely reason?",["Results are personalised using location and search history","One of the colleagues has an older version of the web","The search engine shows each user a random sample","Results depend on the speed of the office network"],"I motori di ricerca personalizzano i risultati (filter bubble). Non c'è una versione del web diversa né un campione casuale.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.1)",2,0],["dg1-008",0,"You find a web page describing a regulation. What should you check first to judge whether it is still up to date?",["The date of publication or last update","The number of times the page was shared","The length of the text on the page","The colours and layout of the site"],"Per una norma conta la data di aggiornamento, perché i testi vengono modificati. Condivisioni, lunghezza e grafica non dicono nulla sull'attualità.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.2)",1,0],["dg1-009",0,"Which file name follows good practice for a document that will be sorted and shared?",["2026-11-16_budget-report_v02.docx","Budget report FINAL new (2).docx","report!!!.docx","Copy of copy of budget.docx"],"Data in formato ISO, parole descrittive e numero di versione rendono il file ordinabile e riconoscibile. Gli altri nomi sono ambigui.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",2,0],["dg1-010",0,"Which of the following file formats uses lossless compression?",["PNG","JPEG","MP3","AAC"],"PNG conserva tutti i dati dell'immagine. JPEG, MP3 e AAC scartano informazione per ridurre le dimensioni.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",2,0],["dg1-011",0,"Which format is designed for the long-term archiving of electronic documents?",["PDF/A","DOCX","RTF","HTML"],"PDF/A è lo standard ISO pensato per la conservazione a lungo termine, perché incorpora font e non dipende da risorse esterne.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",2,0],["dg1-012",0,"What is a CSV file?",["A plain-text file with values separated by delimiters","A compressed archive of several folders and files","An encrypted file protected by a strong password","A video format used in online video conferences"],"CSV è un testo semplice con valori separati da virgole o punti e virgola, leggibile da qualsiasi foglio di calcolo. Non è un archivio né un file cifrato.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",1,0],["dg1-013",0,"Which of the following is metadata of a digital photograph?",["The date and place where it was taken","The faces visible in the picture","The shapes visible in the image","The brightness of its pixels"],"I metadati (EXIF) descrivono il file: data, dispositivo, posizione. Il contenuto visibile dell'immagine non è metadato.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",2,0],["dg1-014",0,"What does the \"3-2-1\" backup rule recommend?",["Three copies, on two types of storage, with one kept off-site","Three copies, in two off-site places, with one encrypted","Three locations, with two passwords and one backup","Three versions, for two users, with one in the cloud"],"La regola 3-2-1 protegge da guasti e da disastri locali: tre copie, due supporti diversi, una copia fuori sede.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",2,0],["dg1-015",0,"A colleague deletes a file from a folder that is synchronised with a cloud service. What usually happens?",["The deletion is copied to the other synchronised devices","The file stays untouched on all other devices","The service asks every user to confirm the deletion","The file is moved to a read-only archive for a year"],"La sincronizzazione replica anche le cancellazioni, quindi non è un backup. La trappola è credere che il cloud conservi sempre una copia.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",3,0],["dg1-016",0,"In a spreadsheet, the formula =B2*$E$1 is copied from row 2 down to row 3. What happens to the reference $E$1?",["It stays pointing to E1","It changes to E2","It changes to F1","It becomes an error"],"Il simbolo $ blocca la riga e la colonna: il riferimento assoluto non cambia quando si copia la formula.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",3,0],["dg1-017",0,"Which formula counts how many cells in A1:A100 are equal to the text \"Yes\"?",["=COUNTIF(A1:A100,\"Yes\")","=SUMIF(A1:A100,\"Yes\")","=COUNT(A1:A100,\"Yes\")","=IF(A1:A100,\"Yes\")"],"COUNTIF conta le celle che soddisfano un criterio. COUNT conta solo i numeri e SUMIF somma, senza contare.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",2,0],["dg1-018",0,"You sort a spreadsheet table by sorting only the \"Surname\" column, without extending the sort to the other columns. What is the result?",["The surnames are reordered but no longer match the other columns","The whole table is reordered correctly whatever you select","The spreadsheet refuses to sort and shows an error message","The other columns are sorted in the reverse order of the first"],"Ordinare una sola colonna sgancia i valori dalle altre colonne della riga. Bisogna selezionare tutta la tabella o una cella al suo interno.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",3,0],["dg1-019",0,"What does applying a filter to a spreadsheet table do?",["It hides the rows that do not meet the condition","It deletes the rows that do not meet the condition","It moves the matching rows to a new file","It changes the values in the matching rows"],"Il filtro nasconde le righe senza eliminarle: i dati restano e tornano visibili togliendo il filtro.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",1,0],["dg1-020",0,"In =VLOOKUP(A2, Table, 3, FALSE), what does the last argument FALSE mean?",["Only an exact match of the lookup value is accepted","The result is returned as a text and not as a number","The search is made in the third column from the right","The lookup stops after the first error found"],"FALSE chiede la corrispondenza esatta. Con TRUE la ricerca è approssimata e richiede la prima colonna ordinata.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.3)",3,0],["dg1-021",0,"In a database search, what does placing OR between two terms usually do?",["It widens the results to pages with either term","It narrows the results to pages with both terms","It excludes pages that contain the second term","It searches only for the exact phrase"],"OR amplia (basta un termine), AND restringe (servono entrambi). La confusione tra i due è la trappola classica.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 1.1)",2,0],["dg1-022",0,"Which description best fits \"open data\"?",["Data that anyone can freely use, reuse and share","Data stored in a file with no password protection","Data a public body publishes only on its intranet","Data that anyone can read free of charge but not reuse"],"Secondo il considerando 16 della direttiva (UE) 2019/1024, i dati aperti sono dati in formato aperto che chiunque può usare, riutilizzare e condividere liberamente. Il solo accesso gratuito non basta.","Directive (EU) 2019/1024, recital 16 (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2019/1024/oj)",2,0],["dg1-023",1,"In an email, what is the usual difference between the To field and the Cc field?",["To is for people who must act, Cc is for people informed","To is for external people, Cc is for internal colleagues","To shows the names to everyone, Cc hides them","To is for messages with attachments, Cc is for those without"],"In A mettiamo chi deve agire, in Cc chi deve solo essere informato. Il campo che nasconde i nomi è Ccn.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 2, competence 2.1)",2,0],["dg1-024",1,"You write to 150 external contacts who do not know each other. How should you enter their addresses?",["In the Bcc field","In the Cc field","In the To field","In the Reply-To field"],"Il campo Ccn evita di rivelare gli indirizzi a tutti e protegge i dati personali. Cc e A li mostrano a ogni destinatario.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.1)",1,0],["dg1-025",1,"A message was sent to 200 people and you only need to answer the sender. Which action is appropriate?",["Use Reply, so only the sender receives the answer","Use Reply All, to keep everyone informed","Use Forward, adding all the recipients again","Use Reply All and put the others in Bcc"],"Rispondi a tutti solo se la risposta serve a tutti. Le altre scelte inondano di messaggi inutili 200 persone.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.1)",1,0],["dg1-026",1,"You are in the Bcc field of a message that also has a sender and recipients in To and Cc. You use Reply All. Who receives your reply?",["The sender and the people in To and Cc","Only the sender of the message","Everyone, including the other Bcc recipients","Only the people in the Cc field"],"Reply All raggiunge mittente, A e Cc visibili, ma non gli altri destinatari in Ccn, che chi risponde non vede.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.1)",3,0],["dg1-027",1,"Which email subject line gives the recipient the most useful information?",["Budget 2027 - approval needed by 20 November","Budget 2027 - some updates and remarks","Budget 2027 - please read as soon as possible","Budget 2027 - details inside the attached file"],"Un oggetto descrittivo indica tema e azione richiesta. Gli altri sono vaghi o allarmistici, e inducono a ignorare il messaggio.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.1)",1,0],["dg1-028",1,"You need to send a 50 MB file to a colleague. What is the best practice?",["Share a link to the file in your organisation's storage","Split the file and send it in many separate emails","Rename the file so that the mail server accepts it","Send it to a personal address that has more space"],"Un link in uno spazio condiviso evita limiti di dimensione e permette di controllare gli accessi. Usare un indirizzo personale espone i dati.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.2)",2,0],["dg1-029",1,"Which content is appropriate for an out-of-office automatic reply?",["Return date and an alternative contact for urgent matters","Destination of the trip and the hotel where you stay","Your home address and your private phone number for emergencies","A detailed list of the projects you are working on now"],"La risposta automatica deve dare data e riferimento alternativo. Dettagli di viaggio o privati aiutano soprattutto chi vuole abusarne.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.1)",2,0],["dg1-030",1,"Three colleagues are drafting a report by emailing copies of the file to each other. What is the best way to avoid conflicting versions?",["Work on one shared online document with version history","Number the email attachments with the date of sending","Ask one person to merge the copies at the end","Let everyone keep a copy and compare them in a meeting"],"Un unico documento condiviso con cronologia delle versioni elimina le copie divergenti. Le altre soluzioni spostano il problema a dopo.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.4)",2,0],["dg1-031",1,"Which feature of a shared document lets you return to an earlier state of the text?",["Version history","Spell checker","Word count","Page layout"],"La cronologia delle versioni conserva gli stati precedenti e permette di ripristinarli. Gli altri strumenti non registrano le modifiche.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.4)",2,0],["dg1-032",1,"What does the \"track changes\" function of a word processor do?",["It records edits so reviewers can accept or reject them","It sends a notification each time the file is opened","It locks the text so that nobody can edit it","It saves every edit in a separate file"],"Le modifiche registrate restano visibili e si possono accettare o rifiutare. Non blocca il testo e non crea file separati.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.4)",1,0],["dg1-033",1,"You want colleagues to give feedback on a draft but not to change its text. Which sharing permission do you choose?",["Comment only","Edit","Owner","Anyone with the link can edit"],"Il permesso di commento consente osservazioni senza modificare il testo. Modifica e proprietà danno controllo troppo ampio.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.4)",2,0],["dg1-034",1,"Which behaviour is good practice in a video conference with many participants?",["Mute your microphone when you are not speaking","Keep the microphone open to react faster","Turn on the recording to help late joiners","Type your remarks in every chat conversation"],"Il microfono spento riduce rumori e echi. Registrare senza avvisare o spammare la chat non è buona pratica.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.5)",1,0],["dg1-035",1,"Before sharing your screen in a meeting, what is the best precaution?",["Share one window and close other apps","Turn off your camera first to save network bandwidth","Share the entire screen so that nothing is missed","Ask the participants to switch off their own notifications"],"Condividere solo la finestra necessaria evita di mostrare messaggi o file riservati. Le altre azioni non proteggono le informazioni.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.2)",2,0],["dg1-036",1,"You plan to record an online meeting. What should you do first?",["Tell the participants and make sure there is a legal basis","Check that the recording is saved in the highest quality","Ask the participants to keep their cameras on","Send the recording to everybody invited to the meeting"],"Registrare significa trattare dati personali: i partecipanti vanno informati e serve una base giuridica ai sensi del GDPR.","Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR), Art. 6 and 13",2,0],["dg1-037",1,"In online messages, what does writing a whole sentence in capital letters usually convey?",["Shouting or strong emphasis","A formal and polite tone","That the text is a quotation","That the message is urgent for the system"],"Nella netiquette il maiuscolo equivale a gridare. Non è un segno di formalità né una priorità tecnica.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.5)",1,0],["dg1-038",1,"You must tell a colleague about a delicate disagreement that could easily be misread. Which channel is the most appropriate?",["A call or a video meeting","A short message in a team chat","An email sent to the whole team","A comment in the shared document"],"Un tema delicato si tratta a voce, dove tono e reazioni si leggono. Chat e commenti pubblici aumentano il rischio di malintesi.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.5)",2,0],["dg1-039",1,"Which description best fits the term \"digital identity\"?",["The information that identifies a person or entity online","The serial number of the computer used by the person","The password that gives access to an account","The set of apps installed on a personal phone"],"L'identità digitale è l'insieme di attributi che identificano una persona in rete. La password è solo uno strumento per provarla.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.6)",2,0],["dg1-040",1,"Which action best helps you to manage your digital footprint?",["Reviewing your privacy settings and what you post","Using a different browser for each website","Deleting your cookies once every year","Having a profile on only one social network"],"Il controllo di impostazioni e contenuti è l'azione diretta sull'impronta digitale. Le altre non riducono ciò che resta visibile.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 2.6)",1,0],["dg1-041",1,"Under the eIDAS Regulation, what legal effect has a qualified electronic signature?",["The same effect as a handwritten signature","An effect limited to the issuing Member State","A lower effect than a handwritten signature","An effect only when a witness confirms it"],"L'articolo 25(2) di eIDAS equipara la firma elettronica qualificata alla firma autografa. Il riconoscimento negli altri Stati membri è previsto separatamente (art. 24a), quindi l'effetto non è limitato allo Stato emittente.","Regulation (EU) No 910/2014, Art. 25(2), consolidated version after Regulation (EU) 2024/1183",3,1],["dg1-042",1,"A Member State public body requires electronic identification for an online service. Under eIDAS, what must it do with identification means from another Member State?",["Recognise those from notified schemes at a sufficient level","Recognise every means issued by any provider in the EU","Recognise them only if the person lives in the first country","Refuse them unless a national identity card is also shown"],"L'articolo 6 impone il riconoscimento dei mezzi di schemi notificati con livello di garanzia almeno pari a quello richiesto. Non è un riconoscimento illimitato né legato alla residenza.","Regulation (EU) No 910/2014, Art. 6(1), consolidated version after Regulation (EU) 2024/1183",3,1],["dg1-043",1,"What does the \"once-only principle\" mean for digital public services?",["Administrations reuse the data already given by citizens","Citizens may submit each online form a single time","Each citizen is allowed one account for all services","A document may be signed with a digital signature only once"],"Con il once-only le amministrazioni riutilizzano i dati già forniti dal cittadino, con il suo consenso. Non limita il numero di invii.","Regulation (EU) 2018/1724, Art. 14 (once-only technical system)",2,0],["dg1-044",1,"Why is it good practice to add alternative text (alt text) to images in documents and web pages?",["Screen reader users can understand what the image shows","The page loads faster than pages without it","The image file becomes smaller when it is sent","The image can be edited later by other readers"],"Il testo alternativo descrive l'immagine a chi usa lo screen reader. Non accelera il caricamento né consente di modificarla.","Directive (EU) 2016/2102; https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376",1,0],["dg1-045",2,"Which password is the best choice for a work account?",["A long, unique passphrase of several unrelated words","A short password with a number and a symbol","Your pet's name followed by your birth year","The same strong password used on all accounts"],"La lunghezza e l'unicità contano più della complicazione. Dati personali e riuso rendono la password facile da indovinare o da rubare.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 4, competence 4.1)",1,0],["dg1-046",2,"What is the main risk of using the same password on several websites?",["A leak from one site gives access to the other accounts","The websites slow down when they share the same password","The password expires faster on each of the other sites","The browser stops offering to save the password for you"],"Il riuso permette il credential stuffing: la password rubata da un sito viene provata sugli altri.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",2,0],["dg1-047",2,"What is the main benefit of a password manager?",["It stores unique passwords behind one master password","It chooses the same password for every website you use","It removes the need for any form of authentication","It sends a copy of the passwords to the IT department"],"Il gestore permette password uniche e lunghe senza doverle ricordare. La master password va protetta bene.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",1,0],["dg1-048",2,"Which combination is a true two-factor authentication?",["A password and a code from an authenticator app","A password and the answer to a security question","A password and a second, different password","A PIN and the answer to a personal question"],"Due fattori devono appartenere a categorie diverse: qualcosa che si sa e qualcosa che si ha. Le altre combinazioni usano due elementi di conoscenza.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",2,0],["dg1-049",2,"Which authentication method is the most resistant to phishing?",["A hardware security key or passkey (FIDO2)","A one-time code received by text message","A one-time code sent to your email address","A security question with a long answer"],"Le chiavi FIDO2 e le passkey legano l'accesso al sito vero, quindi un sito falso non ottiene nulla. Un codice digitato si può farsi dare da un finto portale.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",3,0],["dg1-050",2,"You receive an email from \"IT support\" saying that your account will be locked in one hour unless you click a link. What should you do?",["Not click, and report it through the official channel","Click the link, but do not enter any password","Reply to the sender to ask if the message is genuine","Forward the message to colleagues to warn them"],"Urgenza e minaccia sono segnali tipici del phishing. Anche solo cliccare o rispondere può confermare che l'indirizzo è attivo.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",1,0],["dg1-051",2,"A link in an email reads https://ec.europa.eu.mail-check.net/login. Which domain does the site actually belong to?",["mail-check.net","europa.eu","ec.europa.eu","login"],"Il dominio vero è la parte subito prima del suffisso finale, cioè mail-check.net. Le parole davanti sono solo sottodomini scelti per ingannare.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",2,0],["dg1-052",2,"What characterises \"spear phishing\"?",["A message aimed at one person using personal details","A message sent at random to millions of addresses","A message that spreads by itself through a network","A message that contains neither a link nor an attachment"],"Lo spear phishing è mirato e usa informazioni sulla vittima per sembrare credibile. Il phishing di massa invece è generico.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",2,0],["dg1-053",2,"A caller says he is from the helpdesk and asks you to read out your password to solve a problem. What is the right response?",["Refuse, and contact the helpdesk using the official number","Give the password if he knows your name and office","Give only half of the password and check the reaction","Ask him to call back after you change the password"],"I servizi informatici non chiedono mai la password. Conoscere nome e ufficio non prova l'identità: è ingegneria sociale.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",1,0],["dg1-054",2,"What does ransomware do?",["It encrypts files and demands payment to restore them","It displays advertisements while you browse","It records the keys you type on the keyboard","It copies itself to every device on the network"],"Il ransomware blocca i dati con la cifratura e chiede un riscatto. Gli altri comportamenti descrivono adware, keylogger e worm.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",2,0],["dg1-055",2,"Why is it important to install security updates promptly?",["They fix known vulnerabilities that attackers can exploit","They make the device faster","They remove all the data that is not needed","They stop the device from needing a password"],"Gli aggiornamenti correggono falle note; chi ritarda resta esposto ad attacchi già diffusi. Non sono un modo per velocizzare o per eliminare le password.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",2,0],["dg1-056",2,"What does \"end-to-end encryption\" in a messaging app mean?",["Only the communicating users can read the messages","The provider can read them but not other users","Messages are encrypted only while stored on servers","Messages are encrypted but anyone can decrypt them"],"Con la cifratura end-to-end solo i capi della conversazione hanno le chiavi, nemmeno il fornitore legge i messaggi.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.2)",3,0],["dg1-057",2,"Why enable full-disk encryption on a work laptop?",["The data stays unreadable if the laptop is lost or stolen","The laptop is protected from malware","Deleted files can be recovered afterwards","The laptop uses less battery when it is closed"],"La cifratura del disco protegge la riservatezza dei dati a dispositivo spento o rubato. Non sostituisce antimalware né backup.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",2,0],["dg1-058",2,"You must work on a public Wi-Fi network at a station. What does a VPN do for you in this case?",["It encrypts the traffic between device and VPN server","It protects the device from malware","It makes the public network faster","It stops the network operator from knowing the device is connected"],"La VPN cifra il traffico verso il server VPN, quindi chi controlla la rete non legge il contenuto. Non protegge da malware, non velocizza la rete e non nasconde che il dispositivo è connesso.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",3,0],["dg1-059",2,"A website shows a padlock and its address starts with https. What does this tell you?",["The traffic is encrypted, but the site may be fake","A public authority has checked and approved the site","The site is safe for entering personal information","The site does not collect data or track you"],"Il lucchetto indica solo che il collegamento è cifrato: anche i siti di phishing possono usarlo.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.1)",2,0],["dg1-060",2,"Which of the following is personal data under the GDPR?",["A work email address like name.surname@company.eu","Statistics that cannot be linked to any person","The registration number of a registered company","The average yearly temperature of a city"],"Sono dati personali tutte le informazioni su una persona identificata o identificabile, anche l'indirizzo email di lavoro. I dati veramente anonimi e quelli di società no.","Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR), Art. 4(1)",3,0],["dg1-061",2,"Under the GDPR, within what time should a controller normally notify a personal data breach to the supervisory authority?",["72 hours after becoming aware of it","24 hours after becoming aware of it","7 days after becoming aware of it","30 days after becoming aware of it"],"L'articolo 33 prevede la notifica senza ingiustificato ritardo e, ove possibile, entro 72 ore da quando se ne è venuti a conoscenza.","Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR), Art. 33(1)",2,0],["dg1-062",2,"Which GDPR principle says that only the data needed for the purpose may be collected?",["Data minimisation","Storage limitation","Accuracy","Accountability"],"La minimizzazione (art. 5(1)(c)) impone dati adeguati, pertinenti e limitati allo scopo. La limitazione della conservazione riguarda invece per quanto tempo si tengono.","Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR), Art. 5(1)(c)",2,0],["dg1-063",2,"Which GDPR right allows a person to receive their data in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format?",["The right to data portability","The right of access","The right to erasure","The right to restriction of processing"],"La portabilità (art. 20) permette di ottenere i dati in formato leggibile da macchina e di trasmetterli ad altri. Il diritto di accesso (art. 15) dà una copia ma non è la stessa cosa.","Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR), Art. 20",3,0],["dg1-064",2,"Which habit best supports digital wellbeing?",["Planning screen-free breaks and muting non-essential alerts","Keeping all notifications on to avoid missing anything","Checking work messages in bed to reduce the morning load","Using several screens at once to finish tasks faster"],"Pause senza schermo e meno notifiche riducono stress e distrazioni. Le altre abitudini aumentano il sovraccarico.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.3)",1,0],["dg1-065",2,"Which action most reduces the environmental footprint of your digital devices?",["Using and repairing devices for as long as possible","Replacing your phone every year with a more efficient one","Streaming videos at the highest quality by default","Storing copies of all files in several cloud services"],"La produzione dei dispositivi pesa più dell'uso: allungarne la vita è il gesto più efficace. Cambiare spesso o duplicare i dati aumenta l'impatto.","https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (competence 4.4)",2,0],["dg2-001",3,"A colleague wants a table of contents in a long report that updates automatically when headings change. What should they do?",["Apply built-in heading styles, then insert a table of contents","Type each title and its page number by hand, with dot leaders","Format each title in bold and larger type, then copy it to page one","Add a hyperlink from every title to the first page of its chapter"],"Il sommario automatico si basa sugli stili titolo integrati e si aggiorna con un comando. La formattazione manuale o i link non creano un campo aggiornabile.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3, content creation)",1,0],["dg2-002",3,"What is the main purpose of a mail merge in a word processor?",["To generate personalised copies of a document from a data list","To combine several separate documents into a single long document","To email many people at once without showing the recipients","To merge the edits of several reviewers into the same file"],"La stampa unione abbina un modello a un elenco di dati (nomi, indirizzi) e genera una copia personalizzata per ogni record. Le altre opzioni descrivono attività diverse (unione di file, copia nascosta, revisioni).","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",1,0],["dg2-003",3,"After reviewers have edited a document with Track Changes on, what must the author do to produce a clean final version?",["Accept or reject each tracked change, then stop tracking","Save the file in a different format so the markup is lost","Print the document with the markup hidden and scan it","Delete every comment and keep the tracked changes in place"],"Le modifiche restano nel file finché non vengono accettate o respinte. Nascondere il markup non lo elimina, e cambiare formato non è una procedura affidabile.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",2,0],["dg2-004",3,"Cell B2 contains =A2*$C$1. The formula is copied from B2 to B3. What does B3 contain?",["=A3*$C$1","=A3*$C$2","=A2*$C$1","=A3*C2"],"Il riferimento relativo A2 scorre verso il basso e diventa A3. Il riferimento assoluto $C$1 non cambia. Chi dimentica il simbolo $ sceglie C2.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3, spreadsheets)",2,0],["dg2-005",3,"Which formula counts the cells in A1:A10 that contain a value greater than 50?",["=COUNTIF(A1:A10,\">50\")","=SUMIF(A1:A10,\">50\")","=COUNTA(A1:A10)","=MAX(A1:A10)>50"],"COUNTIF conta le celle che soddisfano una condizione. SUMIF le somma, COUNTA conta tutte le celle non vuote, MAX>50 da' solo vero o falso.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",2,0],["dg2-006",3,"In =VLOOKUP(A2,Table,3,FALSE), what does the last argument FALSE do?",["It requires an exact match for the value being looked up","It returns the value from the third column counted from the right","It ignores empty cells in the first column of the table","It sorts the table before the search is carried out"],"FALSE (o 0) chiede una corrispondenza esatta. Con TRUE la funzione cerca la corrispondenza approssimata e richiede dati ordinati: è la trappola più comune.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",3,0],["dg2-007",3,"What is a PivotTable mainly used for?",["Summarising a data set by moving fields, leaving the source data unchanged","Correcting wrong values in a data set automatically across the whole workbook","Protecting cells that contain formulas so that other users cannot edit them","Checking spelling and grammar in the text cells of a worksheet"],"La tabella pivot riassume e riorganizza i dati originali trascinando i campi. Non corregge, non protegge e non è un collegamento in tempo reale.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",1,0],["dg2-008",3,"A unit wants to show how monthly website traffic evolved over three years. Which chart type is the most suitable?",["A line chart with months on the horizontal axis","A pie chart with one slice for each month","A bar chart with one bar for each visitor","A scatter plot of visits against browser version"],"Per un andamento nel tempo il grafico a linee è la scelta naturale. Il grafico a torta mostra le quote di un totale in un solo momento.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",2,0],["dg2-009",3,"A slide contains a chart that conveys a key message. What helps screen reader users to access it?",["Alternative text describing the chart and its key message","A caption in very small type placed just below the chart","A file name that repeats the full title of the chart itself","A watermark with the name of the author on the picture"],"Il testo alternativo è letto dai lettori di schermo e descrive il contenuto. Un nome di file o una didascalia minuscola non lo sostituiscono.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3, accessibility)",2,0],["dg2-010",3,"Which image format is usually the best choice for a photograph that must be small enough to send by email?",["JPEG","BMP","TIFF","PNG"],"JPEG usa una compressione con perdita molto efficace per le fotografie. BMP e TIFF sono di norma molto più pesanti, PNG è senza perdita e quindi più grande per le foto.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",1,0],["dg2-011",3,"Why is SVG a good format for a logo that will be printed on a business card and on a billboard?",["It describes shapes mathematically, so it scales without loss","It stores a very large grid of pixels, so it prints sharply","It produces smaller files than JPEG when used for photographs","It keeps the colours identical on every printer and screen"],"SVG è vettoriale: descrive le forme con formule e si ingrandisce senza sgranare, dal biglietto da visita al cartellone. Non è pensato per le foto e non memorizza una griglia di pixel.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",2,0],["dg2-012",3,"Which statement about the MP3 audio format is correct?",["It uses lossy compression, discarding some audio data","It is an uncompressed format that keeps every original sample","It is a lossless format like FLAC, but it produces larger files","It is a video container that cannot hold audio-only recordings"],"MP3 comprime con perdita: il file è più piccolo ma parte dell'informazione è scartata. Il formato non compresso tipico è WAV.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",1,0],["dg2-013",3,"What is the difference between a video codec and a video container?",["The codec compresses the video stream; the container packages video, audio and metadata into one file","The codec packages video, audio and metadata into one file; the container compresses the video stream","The codec is used for audio files, while the container is used for video files","The codec describes the screen resolution of the video, while the container describes its frame rate"],"H.264 è un codec, MP4 è un contenitore. La trappola è scambiare i due ruoli.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 3)",3,0],["dg2-014",3,"A photo is published under the licence CC BY-SA 4.0. What must someone do who adapts it and shares the result?",["Credit the author and share the adaptation under a compatible licence","Credit the author, but the adaptation may then be sold under any licence","Ask the author for written permission each time an adaptation is shared","Remove the original credits, because an adaptation is a completely new work"],"BY richiede l'attribuzione, SA (ShareAlike) impone di rilasciare le opere derivate con la stessa licenza o una compatibile.","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",2,0],["dg2-015",3,"Which Creative Commons licence element prevents a work from being used for commercial purposes?",["NC (NonCommercial)","ND (NoDerivatives)","SA (ShareAlike)","BY (Attribution)"],"NC vieta l'uso commerciale. ND vieta le opere derivate, SA impone la stessa licenza, BY richiede il credito.","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/",1,0],["dg2-016",3,"What does the Creative Commons CC0 tool do?",["Rights are waived as far as the law allows, placing the work in the public domain","Free use is allowed if the author is credited and the use is not commercial","The author keeps full copyright, but the work may be viewed for free on the internet","Use is allowed for public bodies, such as schools and libraries, but not for companies"],"CC0 è una rinuncia ai diritti, nei limiti consentiti dalla legge, e non richiede attribuzione. Non è una licenza con condizioni.","https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",3,0],["dg2-017",3,"Under the Berne Convention, when does copyright protection of an original literary work arise?",["Automatically, as soon as the work is created","Once it has been registered with an official body","After the work has been published","When the copyright symbol is shown on the work"],"Secondo l'art. 5(2) della Convenzione di Berna il godimento del diritto d'autore non è subordinato a formalità. Il simbolo (c) e la registrazione non sono condizioni.","Berne Convention, Art. 5(2), https://www.wipo.int/treaties/en/ip/berne/",3,0],["dg2-018",3,"Which statement describes open source software?",["Its source code can be studied, changed and redistributed under a licence","It is distributed free of charge as a compiled program, without its source code","It is released without copyright, so anyone may claim to be its author","It runs on the Linux operating system and its derivatives, but not on Windows"],"Il software open source ha il codice disponibile con una licenza che permette uso, studio, modifica e ridistribuzione. Il diritto d'autore resta e non vale solo per Linux.","https://opensource.org/osd",1,0],["dg2-019",3,"In a simple program: x = 3; x = x + 2; x = x * 2. What value does x hold at the end?",["10","7","12","5"],"3+2=5 e poi 5*2=10. Chi dimentica l'ordine delle istruzioni sceglie 7 o 5.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (programming and logic)",1,0],["dg2-020",3,"What is the final value of total? total = 0; for i = 1, 3, 5: total = total + i",["9","6","15","8"],"Il ciclo passa per i = 1, 3, 5 e somma 1+3+5 = 9. 15 sarebbe la somma da 1 a 5.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (programming and logic)",2,0],["dg2-021",3,"A rule says: if score >= 50 AND attendance >= 80 then result = \"pass\", otherwise \"fail\". A candidate has score 72 and attendance 75. What is the result?",["fail","pass","an error message","no result at all"],"Con AND servono entrambe le condizioni. La frequenza 75 è sotto 80, quindi il ramo \"otherwise\" produce fail.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (programming and logic)",2,0],["dg2-022",3,"What does this algorithm do? max = list[0]; for each item in list: if item > max then max = item; return max",["It returns the largest value in the list","It sorts the list in ascending order","It counts the items that are greater than the first one","It returns the position of the largest value"],"L'algoritmo confronta ogni elemento con il massimo trovato finora e restituisce quel valore. Non ordina e non restituisce la posizione.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (programming and logic)",3,0],["dg2-023",4,"How many bits are there in one byte?",["8","4","10","16"],"Un byte è formato da 8 bit. 4 bit formano un nibble, 16 bit sono due byte.","IEC 80000-13",1,0],["dg2-024",4,"A 2 GB file (1 GB = 1,000 MB) is sent over a connection of 100 megabits per second (Mbit/s), ignoring any overhead. About how long does it take?",["About 2.7 minutes","About 20 seconds","About 27 minutes","About 16 minutes"],"2 GB = 16.000 Mbit, diviso 100 Mbit/s fa 160 secondi, cioè circa 2,7 minuti. La trappola è confondere megabit e megabyte, che da' 20 secondi.","IEC 80000-13",3,0],["dg2-025",4,"In the decimal (SI) convention, how many megabytes are there in one gigabyte?",["1,000","1,024","100","10,000"],"Nel sistema SI il prefisso giga vale 1.000 volte mega. 1.024 vale per il gibibyte e il mebibyte (convenzione binaria).","BIPM, SI prefixes, https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-prefixes; IEC 80000-13",2,0],["dg2-026",4,"A desktop computer does not start at all: no lights, no fan noise. What should be checked first?",["Whether the power cable is plugged in and the socket works","Whether the operating system must be reinstalled from scratch","Whether the hard disk has to be replaced with a new one","Whether the BIOS firmware needs an update to a newer version"],"Si parte dalla causa più semplice e meno costosa: l'alimentazione. Reinstallare o sostituire componenti viene dopo.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5, problem solving)",1,0],["dg2-027",4,"A user can open a website by typing its IP address, but not by typing its domain name. Which service is the most likely cause?",["DNS","DHCP","NAT","SMTP"],"Il DNS traduce i nomi in indirizzi IP. Se l'IP funziona la rete è a posto e il guasto riguarda la risoluzione dei nomi. SMTP è per la posta.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",2,0],["dg2-028",4,"During a video call over Wi-Fi the image keeps freezing. A speed test shows high delay and packet loss. Which action will most likely help?",["Move closer to the access point or use a network cable","Raise the screen resolution of the computer display","Clear the autofill and saved passwords of the browser","Add more storage space to the internal hard disk"],"Perdita di pacchetti e latenza indicano un segnale debole. Avvicinarsi o usare il cavo migliora la connessione, le altre azioni non toccano la rete.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",1,0],["dg2-029",4,"What does the \"ping\" command show?",["Whether a host is reachable and the round-trip time","How much bandwidth the link between two hosts has","Whether the website certificate is still valid","Which network ports are open on a remote computer"],"Ping invia richieste di echo e misura il tempo di andata e ritorno. Non misura la banda e non analizza le porte.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",2,0],["dg2-030",4,"An application has stopped responding. Which is the least disruptive way to close it?",["Force it to quit from Task Manager or Activity Monitor","Hold the power button to shut the whole computer down","Uninstall the application and install it again at once","Delete the folder where the application keeps its settings"],"Chiudere solo il programma bloccato evita di perdere il lavoro nelle altre applicazioni. Spegnere o disinstallare è sproporzionato.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",1,0],["dg2-031",4,"The disk of a laptop is almost full. What is a sensible first step to find what is using the space?",["Use a disk usage tool to list the largest folders and files","Format the drive and restore the files from a backup later","Defragment the disk so that it frees space for new files","Compress the entire system folder to save a lot of space"],"Prima si individua cosa occupa spazio. Formattare è distruttivo, la deframmentazione non libera spazio e comprimere il sistema può causare problemi.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",1,0],["dg2-032",4,"In most Windows applications, which keyboard shortcut undoes the last action?",["Ctrl + Z","Ctrl + Y","Ctrl + X","Ctrl + A"],"Ctrl+Z annulla. Ctrl+Y ripete l'azione annullata, Ctrl+X taglia, Ctrl+A seleziona tutto.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",1,0],["dg2-033",4,"Which description matches Software as a Service (SaaS)?",["A ready-to-use application delivered over the internet and managed by the provider","Rented virtual servers on which the customer installs its own systems","An environment in which developers deploy code without managing servers","An application installed on a local server and maintained by the customer's IT team"],"Nel SaaS il fornitore gestisce tutto e il cliente usa l'applicazione. La seconda opzione è IaaS, la terza è PaaS, la quarta è un'installazione locale.","https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/145/final",2,0],["dg2-034",4,"Why is a synchronised cloud folder not a complete backup?",["A deletion or corruption made locally is copied to all synchronised copies","Synchronised files are not encrypted while they travel over the network","Cloud providers keep one copy of each file, on a single server in one building","Synchronisation does not work for large files, such as videos and databases"],"La sincronizzazione replica anche gli errori, comprese le cancellazioni. Un backup conserva versioni separate nel tempo.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 4, safety)",2,0],["dg2-035",4,"What does the \"3-2-1\" backup rule recommend?",["Three copies of the data, on two types of storage, with one copy off-site","Three copies on two different computers, all kept in the same office","Two copies of the data, on three types of storage, with one of them encrypted","Three full backups per week, two per day and one archive per month"],"La regola 3-2-1 prevede tre copie, su due tipi di supporto, di cui una fuori sede. Le altre varianti ne copiano i numeri ma non il senso.","CISA, Data Backup Options (regola 3-2-1), https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/publications/data_backup_options.pdf",3,0],["dg2-036",4,"What is the main role of an operating system?",["It manages the hardware and provides services to applications","It translates website names into IP addresses for the browser","It removes all malware automatically without any user action","It stores the personal files of the user on the internet"],"Il sistema operativo gestisce processore, memoria, dischi e periferiche e offre servizi ai programmi. Tradurre i nomi è compito del DNS.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",2,0],["dg2-037",4,"What does a ZIP file do?",["It packs files into a single compressed archive","It encrypts the files with a strong password by default","It converts word processor documents into the PDF format","It deletes duplicate files from the entire hard disk"],"ZIP riunisce e comprime i file senza perdita. La cifratura è opzionale, non è il comportamento predefinito.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",2,0],["dg2-038",4,"What is a macro in an office application?",["A recorded sequence of actions that can be replayed","A document template with ready-made layout and styles","A very large spreadsheet with many sheets and formulas","A security setting that blocks links to external files"],"Una macro automatizza operazioni ripetitive. Un modello è un'altra cosa. Le macro vanno attivate solo da fonti fidate perché possono contenere codice dannoso.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",2,0],["dg2-039",4,"A final 40-page report with images must look identical on every device and must not be edited by readers. Which format is the best choice?",["PDF","DOCX","TXT","RTF"],"Il PDF conserva l'impaginazione ed è pensato per la lettura. DOCX e RTF si possono modificare e possono cambiare aspetto, TXT perde formattazione e immagini.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",1,0],["dg2-040",4,"A team must collect structured answers from 300 people and analyse them quickly. Which tool is the most suitable?",["An online form whose answers are stored in a spreadsheet","A shared presentation where each person adds a slide","A group email thread with replies collected by hand","A word processor document sent around with tracked changes"],"Il modulo online raccoglie risposte uniformi e le mette in una tabella pronta per l'analisi. Le altre soluzioni richiedono molto lavoro manuale.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",1,0],["dg2-041",4,"A shared network printer works for everyone except one user, whose jobs stay in the queue. What is the most logical first step?",["Clear that user's print queue and check the selected printer","Replace the toner cartridge of the shared network printer","Reinstall the operating system on every computer in the office","Replace the network switch of the whole building floor"],"Il guasto riguarda un solo utente, quindi si guarda il suo computer: coda e stampante selezionata. Toner e switch toccherebbero tutti.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",2,0],["dg2-042",4,"What is the best general approach when troubleshooting a technical problem?",["Change one thing at a time and test after each change","Apply several possible fixes together to save time","Reinstall the whole system before looking for the cause","Wait until the problem has occurred at least three times"],"Cambiando una cosa per volta si capisce cosa ha risolto (o peggiorato) il problema. Cambiare tutto insieme rende impossibile la diagnosi.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",2,0],["dg2-043",4,"Task Manager shows memory use at 95% with dozens of browser tabs open, and the computer is slow. What is the most direct fix?",["Close unused tabs and applications","Switch the Wi-Fi to the 5 GHz band","Empty the recycle bin of the computer","Reset the Wi-Fi router and modem"],"La lentezza viene dalla memoria quasi satura: liberarla chiudendo ciò che non serve è la soluzione più diretta. Wi-Fi e router riguardano la rete.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",1,0],["dg2-044",4,"What is safe mode of an operating system mainly used for?",["Starting with minimal drivers and services to find faults","Starting with the user's personal files encrypted by the system","Browsing the web privately without being tracked by websites","Running applications inside an isolated sandbox for safety"],"La modalità provvisoria avvia solo il necessario, così si capisce se il guasto dipende da driver o programmi aggiunti. Non è una modalità di privacy.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 5)",2,0],["dg2-045",5,"What does a generative AI model do?",["It creates new text or images from patterns learned in training","It retrieves only exact pages from a stored index of documents","It applies fixed rules that a programmer wrote for every single case","It encrypts data so that nobody can read it without the right key"],"I modelli generativi creano contenuti nuovi a partire da schemi appresi. Un motore di ricerca recupera, un sistema a regole segue istruzioni fisse.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (emerging tech); https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/artificial-intelligence",1,0],["dg2-046",5,"What is meant by a \"hallucination\" of a language model?",["A plausible-sounding answer that is false or invented","A refusal to answer because the question seems risky","A slow response caused by heavy load on the servers","A reply that repeats the training texts word for word"],"L'allucinazione è un contenuto verosimile ma inventato. Per questo i fatti vanno controllati su fonti affidabili.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/artificial-intelligence",1,0],["dg2-047",5,"Which practice usually improves the answers of a generative AI assistant?",["Stating the context, the task, the format and any limits","Using as few words as possible, to keep the request short","Asking several unrelated tasks in one single sentence","Pasting entire personal files so the model has more context"],"Un prompt chiaro con contesto, compito e formato produce risposte migliori. Incollare file personali è anche un rischio per la riservatezza.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (emerging tech)",2,0],["dg2-048",5,"A colleague wants to paste a confidential draft contract into a public AI chatbot to get a summary. What is the main risk?",["The text may be kept or reused outside the organisation's control","The chatbot will refuse to read any document marked as confidential","The document will lose its original formatting and page layout","The chatbot will automatically sign the contract on your behalf"],"In un servizio pubblico il testo può essere conservato o usato dal fornitore: si perde il controllo su dati riservati. Le altre opzioni non sono rischi reali.","https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection_en",2,0],["dg2-049",5,"An official uses a chatbot to prepare a briefing and receives a confident answer with several references. What should be done before using it?",["Check the facts and references against reliable sources","Use it, because the answer includes several references","Ask the chatbot again and use it if the answer is consistent","Use it if the tone is formal and the text well structured"],"I riferimenti possono essere inventati e la coerenza fra risposte non prova che siano vere. I fatti si verificano alla fonte.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/artificial-intelligence",2,0],["dg2-050",5,"Why can an AI system produce results that are biased against some groups?",["It learns from data that may reflect existing inequalities","Its developers insert the bias on purpose to favour some groups","It is too slow to take all of the available data into account","It uses more electricity when it processes data about some groups"],"I modelli imparano dai dati: se i dati riflettono disparità storiche, il sistema può riprodurle, anche senza intenzione.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/artificial-intelligence",2,0],["dg2-051",5,"What characterises supervised machine learning?",["The model learns from examples labelled with answers","A person supervises the model during every calculation","The model follows a fixed set of programmed if-then rules","The model finds groups in the data without any labels"],"Nell'apprendimento supervisionato i dati sono etichettati. Trovare gruppi senza etichette è apprendimento non supervisionato.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/artificial-intelligence",2,0],["dg2-052",5,"What is the \"context window\" of a large language model?",["The maximum amount of text the model can consider at once","The browser window in which the conversation is shown","The list of websites the model is allowed to visit online","The period of time covered by the training data set"],"La finestra di contesto è il limite di testo (domanda, documenti, risposta) che il modello considera insieme. Oltre quel limite l'informazione viene persa.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/artificial-intelligence",3,0],["dg2-053",5,"How is open data best described?",["Data anyone can access, use and share, usually machine-readable","Data that has been stored in a cloud service of an institution","Data that is posted publicly on social networks and websites","Data from which personal information has been removed internally"],"Dati aperti vuol dire accessibili e riutilizzabili da tutti, di norma in formato leggibile da una macchina. Il cloud o i social non li rendono aperti.","https://data.europa.eu/en",2,0],["dg2-054",5,"Which format is the most suitable to publish a table as machine-readable open data?",["CSV","A scanned PDF of the printed table","A PNG screenshot of the table","A word processor document with the table"],"Il CSV è un formato aperto e leggibile dai programmi. Un PDF scansionato o uno screenshot sono immagini: non si possono elaborare direttamente.","https://data.europa.eu/en",1,0],["dg2-055",5,"Which EU act sets common rules for the re-use of public sector information and the publication of open data?",["Directive (EU) 2019/1024","Regulation (EU) 2016/679","Directive 2001/29/EC","Regulation (EU) No 910/2014"],"La direttiva (UE) 2019/1024 è la direttiva sui dati aperti e sul riutilizzo dell'informazione del settore pubblico. 2016/679 è il GDPR, 2001/29 il diritto d'autore, 910/2014 l'identificazione elettronica.","https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2019/1024/oj/eng",3,0],["dg2-056",5,"What is a typical Internet of Things (IoT) device?",["A physical object with sensors that connects to a network","A program that protects a company network from intruders","A protocol used by browsers to display web pages","A service that stores personal files in the cloud"],"Un dispositivo IoT è un oggetto fisico connesso, per esempio un termostato intelligente. Gli altri esempi sono software o servizi.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (emerging tech)",2,0],["dg2-057",5,"Which is a common security weakness of IoT devices?",["Weak default passwords and firmware that is rarely updated","Short battery life, which is a security vulnerability in itself","Use of wired connections that cannot be encrypted","Large screens that expose data to people nearby"],"Credenziali predefinite deboli e firmware non aggiornato sono tra le cause più frequenti di attacchi ai dispositivi connessi.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 4, safety)",2,0],["dg2-058",5,"Which description fits a blockchain?",["A shared ledger of linked blocks, hard to alter afterwards","A central database run by one authority that may edit any record at will","A compression method that makes very large files much smaller","A method to encrypt email messages from sender to recipient"],"La blockchain è un registro condiviso, in blocchi concatenati con funzioni crittografiche, che rende difficile alterare le registrazioni passate.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/european-blockchain-services-infrastructure",3,0],["dg2-059",5,"What is a smart contract on a blockchain?",["A program on a blockchain that runs when conditions are met","A legal contract signed with a qualified electronic signature","A contract for renting cloud hosting for a blockchain node","A paper contract that has been scanned and then hashed"],"Lo smart contract è codice eseguito dalla rete al verificarsi delle condizioni. Non è di per sé un contratto firmato né un servizio di hosting.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/european-blockchain-services-infrastructure",2,0],["dg2-060",5,"In a blockchain, what role does a hash of a block play?",["A fixed-length fingerprint that changes if the data change","A secret password that lets the owner reverse a transaction","A backup copy of the whole block kept on a second server","A list of all the users who have read or edited the block"],"La funzione di hash produce un'impronta di lunghezza fissa: se i dati cambiano, l'impronta cambia, e questo permette di accorgersi delle manomissioni.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/european-blockchain-services-infrastructure",3,0],["dg2-061",5,"Why is continuous learning especially important for digital skills?",["Tools and practices change quickly, so skills need regular updating","Digital skills are acquired at school and stay valid for a whole career","Certificates in digital skills lose their value after one year","New tools work in the same way as the old ones, so nothing needs relearning"],"Gli strumenti digitali evolvono in fretta: DigComp stesso è un quadro aggiornato nel tempo. Le competenze vanno rinnovate con regolarità.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (introduction)",2,0],["dg2-062",5,"What is a deepfake?",["AI-made media imitating a real person's face or voice","An encrypted video format used by public institutions and banks","A phishing email that hides links inside very long addresses","A video recorded with an unusually high resolution and frame rate"],"Un deepfake è un contenuto audio o video sintetico che imita una persona reale. È un rischio di disinformazione e frode.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/artificial-intelligence",2,0],["dg2-063",5,"A striking image of a public event is circulating and may have been generated by AI. Which check is the most reliable first step?",["Run a reverse image search to find the original source","Trust it, because it has already been shared by many people","Compare the size of the image file with similar pictures","Zoom in: if the picture is pixelated, it is certainly fake"],"La ricerca inversa per immagine aiuta a trovare l'origine e il contesto. La diffusione o la dimensione del file non provano nulla.","DigComp 2.2, https://data.europa.eu/doi/10.2760/115376 (area 1, information literacy)",2,0],["dg2-064",5,"What distinguishes a qubit in quantum computing from a classical bit?",["It can be in a combination of 0 and 1 until measured","It can store eight different values at the same time","It is always faster than a classical bit in every task","It is a classical bit that is protected by encryption"],"Il qubit sfrutta la sovrapposizione di stati. Non è vero che sia sempre più veloce: il vantaggio vale solo per certi problemi.","https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/quantum",3,0],["dg2-065",5,"What does the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689) rely on as its main approach?",["Obligations that depend on the level of risk of the AI system","A general ban on AI, with a few authorised exceptions","Rules that depend on the size of the company selling the system","Rules that depend on the country where the system is built"],"Il regolamento segue un approccio basato sul rischio: pratiche vietate, requisiti per i sistemi ad alto rischio, obblighi di trasparenza. Non vieta l'IA in generale e non dipende da dimensione o paese dell'impresa.","https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj/eng",3,0]]};
